<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Publicly available data | Jidong Yang</title><link>http://127.0.0.1:8830/datasets/</link><atom:link href="http://127.0.0.1:8830/datasets/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><description>Publicly available data</description><generator>Wowchemy (https://wowchemy.com)</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 23 May 2022 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><image><url>http://127.0.0.1:8830/media/icon_hubd2f80d78884ba0239fa1548e84cd589_19268_512x512_fill_lanczos_center_3.png</url><title>Publicly available data</title><link>http://127.0.0.1:8830/datasets/</link></image><item><title>Shengli Model</title><link>http://127.0.0.1:8830/datasets/shengli-model/</link><pubDate>Mon, 23 May 2022 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://127.0.0.1:8830/datasets/shengli-model/</guid><description>&lt;p>
&lt;figure >
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="./shengli_model.png" alt="Geological structure of the Shengli oilfield model" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>This is a model that is similar to the actual geological structure of the Shengli oil field.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Velocity and attenuation models of the BP gas reservoir</title><link>http://127.0.0.1:8830/datasets/velocity-and-attenuation-models-of-bp-gas-reservoir/</link><pubDate>Tue, 05 Feb 2019 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>http://127.0.0.1:8830/datasets/velocity-and-attenuation-models-of-bp-gas-reservoir/</guid><description>&lt;p>This is a gas reservoir model with both P-wave velocity and Qp parameters. We build this model by modifying the right part of the original BP model, which can be used for seismic modeling, migration and inversion study.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The model files are RSF format. The detailed RSF format is shown in the Madagascar software website (&lt;a href="https://www.ahay.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.ahay.org&lt;/a>).&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Access to the data and a detailed description can &lt;a href="https://github.com/JidongYangUPC/Velocity-and-attenuation-models-of-BP-Gas-Reservoir1.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">click this link.&lt;/a>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure >
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="./vp.png" alt="P-wave velocity model of the BP gas reservoir" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
&lt;p>
&lt;figure >
&lt;div class="d-flex justify-content-center">
&lt;div class="w-100" >&lt;img src="./qp.png" alt="P-wave quality factor (Qp) model of the BP gas reservoir" loading="lazy" data-zoomable />&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;/figure>
&lt;/p>
